  "notes": [
    "Chaos run: The first worker takes an extra 5 s before it answers and the header timeout (8 s) is above that: its requests are slow but succeed, so a breaker must not open (the false-positive check).",
    "What this embedded mock cluster cannot show here: The delay holds the mock's slot but not a CPU: a real slow worker (a long prefill, a GPU stall) also degrades its neighbours on the same device, which a mock cannot.",
    "Windows follow when the fault was really applied and cleared. Gateway counters (attempts per request, retries) are read at the tick that opens and closes a window (every 1s), so an attempt of a request in flight at a boundary falls in the next window; the per-request figures come from the clients.",
    "Closed-loop clients: 14 for the whole run on 32 request slots (24 left serving). Closed-loop clients wait for each response, so a failing worker also slows the offered load.",
    "Load average (1, 5 and 15 minutes) at the start of the run: 3.58 3.42 3.83; at the end: 3.02 3.25 3.74."
  ],
